  "scope": "Authenticated plain-read permission refusals and bounded physical-process resource ownership. Broader routing fails; no complete OPT or CG qualification.",
  "mechanism": "A validated plain-read header that lacks namespace access receives a request-tag/route/sequence/TLS-exporter-bound signed refusal after bounded body authentication. Metadata-only ingress uses its existing process epoch and the peer incoming query bank shared with any later regular pool. It receives no namespace permission or query sender worker.",
  "preserved_contracts": [
    "Original node/peer byte and item limits, I/O deadlines, process and rooted trust fences remain. Unknown/superseded physical sources retain closure/refusal.",
    "Only plain Query may emit or interpret this read refusal. Commands, event queries and all other purposes reject the marker as Protocol; uncertain writes retain their existing identity, receipt reconciliation and acknowledgement proofs.",
    "Response MAC and exact request binding precede body authentication and refusal interpretation. Cellar format markers remain 1; matching peers must be rebuilt.",
    "An incomplete denied request retains the original node and peer charge until physical I/O exits. Explicit TLS shutdown passes selected actual transport checks; isolated close timing varies, so no complete physical-process cancellation/fairness oracle follows."
  ],
